<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fall of the Western Roman Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/476">476 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a> is conventionally dated to 476 CE, when the Germanic commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> deposed the last western emperor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a>. It was the culmination of a long period of invasion, civil war and fiscal decline, while the eastern half of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> survived as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fall-of-the-western-roman-empire.jpg" alt="Fall of the Western Roman Empire" width="320" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roke (d) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Republic_Empire_map.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
